cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "nanoentropy: Nanopore methylation entropy analysis toolkit"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-04-29"
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/uribertocchitau/nanoentropy"
url: "https://github.com/uribertocchitau/nanoentropy"
abstract: >-
  nanoentropy is a Streamlit GUI and CLI for nanopore methylation entropy
  analysis. It computes methylation entropy (ME), mean methylation level
  (MML), and coverage bedgraphs from modkit-extracted CpG calls, performs
  block segmentation, runs GO enrichment via an R bridge, and produces
  track, scatter, and distribution plots. Three entropy modes are supported:
  True-mC (5hmC -> C), Bisulfite-equivalent, and Ternary (3-state).
